(Reflection Notes: Through this plan, I learned that UniMart is currently a well-reasoned idea, not a proven) Tj
T* (business. The core problem is that first-year hostel students waste time and money visiting multiple shops for) Tj
T* (basic items. It is based on my own observation and informal conversations, and none of it has been tested with) Tj
T* (real data yet. The most important thing I learned is that the riskiest assumption is not whether students like the) Tj
T* (idea, but whether they will order repeatedly instead of using nearby shops, Amazon or WhatsApp groups. My) Tj
T* (market size and revenue numbers are also estimates, and I need to replace them with real data.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I also learned to narrow my focus. I started with a broad student marketplace, but I now see that the strongest) Tj
T* (starting point is first-year DGU hostel students, who are new to Dehradun, clustered in one place and easy to) Tj
T* (reach through WhatsApp groups. I also decided to keep the first version very small: a WhatsApp group and) Tj
T* (Google Form for daily essentials, with the app, payments and student-to-student resale left for later.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (My next validation actions, in order of priority, are:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Weeks 1 to 2: Survey 30 to 50 hostel students and interview 8 to 10 first-years about how often they shop for) Tj
T* (basics, how much time and money it costs, and whether they would try a one-stop option \(tests the core friction\).) Tj
T* (Weeks 1 to 2: Collect quotes from 2 to 3 local wholesalers or suppliers for the 15 to 20 most-ordered items, and) Tj
T* (compare them with nearby shop prices \(tests whether the 15 to 20% margin is realistic\).) Tj
T* (Weeks 3 to 6: Run the 30-day pilot in one or two hostel blocks using a WhatsApp group and Google Form, with) Tj
T* (about 50 orders as the target \(tests the MVP\).) Tj
T* (During the pilot: Track sign-ups and orders by channel using separate QR codes, to measure the real cost of) Tj
T* (acquiring each customer.) Tj
T* (End of pilot: Measure the repeat-order rate. If at least 30% of first-time buyers order again, I will continue and add) Tj
T* (the textbook exchange. If not, I will change the product range, pricing or delivery model, or narrow the segment) Tj
T* (further.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I will update my market size, revenue and cost numbers using the real data from these steps, and only move to a) Tj
T* (full app after demand is proven.) Tj
